From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3: Use the HW_GK3 Wi-Fi board data

The NTM_TW220 board data selected by the calibration variant pins the
WCN6855 firmware to the US regulatory domain. The firmware never takes
a country from 802.11d with it, and for every country set from user
space (US, AU, CN, DE and JP were tried) it allows the 2.4 GHz band
only up to channel 11, with the rule ending at 2472 MHz. Channels 12
and 13 stay disabled and networks on them cannot be found, although
this tablet is sold in China, where both channels are in common use.

linux-firmware has the NTM_TW220 data also for the Lenovo X13s under
qmi-chip-id=18; HW_GK3 shares the data of the X13s qmi-chip-id=2
entry. With it the firmware takes the country of nearby access points
and allows channels 12 and 13 for passive scanning. Against NTM_TW220,
5 GHz gave the same signal and iperf3 throughput over three interleaved
rounds, and 2.4 GHz showed no difference; 6 GHz was not compared.
Dropping the variant is not an option: the generic qmi-chip-id=18 data
it falls back to is about 22 dB weaker.

linux-firmware lists HW_GK3 only under qmi-chip-id=2, while this chip
reports chip_id 0x12, so board-2.bin needs a qmi-chip-id=18 name for
the same data. The device firmware step adds it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [needs a board-2.bin name that linux-firmware lacks]
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
index 18934eb7a..8f29b189b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
@@ -1015,8 +1015,11 @@ wifi@0 {
 		vddrfa1p2-supply = <&vreg_pmu_rfa_1p2>;
 		vddrfa1p8-supply = <&vreg_pmu_rfa_1p7>;
 
-		/* HACK: qmi-chip-id=18 */
-		qcom,calibration-variant = "NTM_TW220";
+		/*
+		 * linux-firmware lists HW_GK3 only under qmi-chip-id=2; this chip
+		 * reports 18, so board-2.bin carries an extra qmi-chip-id=18 name.
+		 */
+		qcom,calibration-variant = "HW_GK3";
 	};
 };
 
